- [x] Added safe fallback when `quietHours` is absent or malformed (`enabled !== true` or invalid `HH:MM` times): notification displays.
- [x] Limited `now` usage to quiet-hours deterministic evaluation; default runtime uses current time when contract not active.

### Quiet-Hours Payload Contract (explicit)
- Push payload may include:
  - `quietHours: { enabled: true, start: "HH:MM", end: "HH:MM" }`
  - optional `now: string` (ISO date-time) for deterministic suppression checks
- Suppression applies only when quiet-hours contract is valid.
- If `quietHours` is absent/invalid, fallback is **display notification**.

